{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.util.stream.IntStream;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        FastScanner in = new FastScanner(System.in);\n        PrintWriter out = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n        new Solver().run(in, out);\n        out.close();\n    }\n\n    static class Solver {\n        void run(FastScanner in, PrintWriter out) {\n            int n = in.nextInt();\n            if (n > 11) {\n                out.println(\"0\");\n                return;\n            }\n            Point[] pts = new Point[n];\n            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n                pts[i] = new Point(in.nextInt(), in.nextInt(), in.nextInt(), in.nextInt(), in.nextInt());\n            }\n            List<Integer> good = new ArrayList<>();\n            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n                final int fi = i;\n                boolean bad = IntStream.range(0, n).anyMatch(j ->\n                        IntStream.range(0, n).anyMatch(k -> {\n                            if (fi != j && fi != k && j != k) {\n                                Point v1 = pts[j].sub(pts[fi]);\n                                Point v2 = pts[k].sub(pts[fi]);\n                                return acute(v1, v2);\n                            }\n                            return false;\n                        })\n                );\n                if (!bad) good.add(i + 1);\n            }\n            if (good.isEmpty()) {\n                out.println(\"0\");\n            } else {\n                out.println(good.size());\n                good.forEach(out::println);\n            }\n        }\n\n        static boolean acute(Point a, Point b) {\n            double dot = a.a*b.a + a.b*b.b + a.c*b.c + a.d*b.d + a.e*b.e;\n            double ang = Math.acos(dot / (a.mag() * b.mag()));\n            return Math.toDegrees(ang) < 90;\n        }\n    }\n\n    static class Point {\n        int a, b, c, d, e;\n        Point(int a, int b, int c, int d, int e) {\n            this.a = a; this.b = b; this.c = c; this.d = d; this.e = e;\n        }\n        Point sub(Point o) {\n            return new Point(a-o.a, b-o.b, c-o.c, d-o.d, e-o.e);\n        }\n        double mag() {\n            return Math.sqrt(a*a + b*b + c*c + d*d + e*e);\n        }\n    }\n\n    static class FastScanner {\n        BufferedReader reader;\n        StringTokenizer tokenizer;\n        FastScanner(InputStream stream) {\n            reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(stream), 32768);\n            tokenizer = null;\n        }\n        String next() {\n            while (tokenizer == null || !tokenizer.hasMoreTokens()) {\n                try {\n                    tokenizer = new StringTokenizer(reader.readLine());\n                } catch (IOException e) {\n                    throw new RuntimeException(e);\n                }\n            }\n            return tokenizer.nextToken();\n        }\n        int nextInt() { return Integer.parseInt(next()); }\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nimport math\n\nclass Point:\n    def __init__(self, a, b, c, d, e):\n        self.a = a\n        self.b = b\n        self.c = c\n        self.d = d\n        self.e = e\n\n    def sub(self, other):\n        return Point(self.a - other.a, self.b - other.b, self.c - other.c,\n                     self.d - other.d, self.e - other.e)\n\n    def mag(self):\n        return math.sqrt(self.a*self.a + self.b*self.b + self.c*self.c +\n                         self.d*self.d + self.e*self.e)\n\ndef acute(v1, v2):\n    dot = v1.a*v2.a + v1.b*v2.b + v1.c*v2.c + v1.d*v2.d + v1.e*v2.e\n    mag_product = v1.mag() * v2.mag()\n    # Clamp to avoid floating point errors\n    cos_angle = max(-1.0, min(1.0, dot / mag_product))\n    angle = math.acos(cos_angle)\n    return math.degrees(angle) < 90.0\n\ndef solve():\n    data = list(map(int, sys.stdin.buffer.read().split()))\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n = data[0]\n    if n > 11:\n        print(0)\n        return\n    pts = []\n    idx = 1\n    for _ in range(n):\n        a, b, c, d, e = data[idx:idx+5]\n        pts.append(Point(a, b, c, d, e))\n        idx += 5\n\n    good = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        bad = False\n        for j in range(n):\n            if j == i:\n                continue\n            for k in range(n):\n                if k == i or k == j:\n                    continue\n                v1 = pts[j].sub(pts[i])\n                v2 = pts[k].sub(pts[i])\n                if acute(v1, v2):\n                    bad = True\n                    break\n            if bad:\n                break\n        if not bad:\n            good.append(i + 1)\n\n    if not good:\n        print(0)\n    else:\n        print(len(good))\n        for idx in good:\n            print(idx)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n1.0\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-2.3841830625315197e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -2.15766